.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH lint 1  "lint " 
.SH NAME
lint \- Lint Lexicon Markdown files — checks spec compliance and common drafting errors (unused defined terms, duplicate definitions, broken cross\-references, missing exhibit files, ...) without generating output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlint\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-style\fR] [\fB\-\-numbering\-convention\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-rules\fR] [\fB\-\-fix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIINPUTS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lint Lexicon Markdown files — checks spec compliance and common drafting errors (unused defined terms, duplicate definitions, broken cross\-references, missing exhibit files, ...) without generating output
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format: human\-readable text, JSON (for editors, CI, and AI agents), or GitHub Actions annotations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable diagnostics, one per line
.IP \(bu 2
json: Structured JSON report on stdout
.IP \(bu 2
github: GitHub Actions workflow\-command annotations
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Fail on warnings as well as errors (exit code 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Disable a rule by code (repeatable; merged with [lint] ignore in style.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Hide diagnostics below this severity
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRerror, warning, info]
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR
Style configuration file (TOML; supplies the [lint] section and numbering convention). If not specified, searches for style.toml next to each input, then in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lexicon/
.TP
\fB\-\-numbering\-convention\fR \fI<NUMBERING_CONVENTION>\fR
Numbering convention used when formatting clause references in messages
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRcommonwealth, decimal, us\-traditional]
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-rules\fR
List all lint rules (code, default severity, description) and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-fix\fR
Rewrite fixable findings in place. Currently normalises hand\-numbered ordinals (10. and wider) to 1., dedenting each item\*(Aqs content to match. Verified structurally before writing; a rewrite that would change the document is abandoned
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIINPUTS\fR]
Input Lexicon Markdown file(s)
